    "title": "Gabon Holds First Elections After Military Coup",
    "text": "• Gabon held its first legislative and local elections on Saturday.\n• The elections are the first since a military coup in 2023.\n• The coup ended a 50-year political dynasty in the country.\n• More than 900,000 Gabonese citizens are eligible to vote.\n• Voters are electing parliament members and local councilors.\n• The officials being replaced were appointed by the military after the coup.",
